      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im having a bit of a headache with aws. i'm trying to get a lambda function to write logs to an s3 bucket but i keep getting an Access Denied error in the cloudwatch logs even though i thought i set the policy up right. \n\ncan u take a look at this policy?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-log-bucket-12345\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The policy you've shared only explicitly allows the `s3:PutObject` action and does not cover other required permissions for Lambda to create and drain log groups and streams. For Lambda to write logs to CloudWatch, you need permissions related to CloudWatch as well. You might need to add additional statements like \"logs:CreateLogStream\", \"logs:PutLogEvents\", and \"logs:CreateLogGroup\" to your policy, or use an AWS managed policy like `AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole` that provides the necessary permissions by default. Review the permissions and make sure they fit your use case.",
